\title{Vagla Language Resources for K-12 Curriculum Development}
\author{Compiled by Claude Sonnet 5 (claude-sonnet-5) for Andr\'as Kornai}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Vagla (ISO 639-3: vag) is a Gur language of Ghana's Savannah Region with about 14,000 speakers. It is written in the Latin alphabet, with doubled letters for long vowels.
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers or school textbooks were found in search results.
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Vagla--English, English--Vagla dictionary by Marjorie Crouch and Patricia Herbert (GILLBT), web edition on Webonary; print editions 1981 and 2002 are listed in Glottolog. \url{https://www.webonary.org/vagla/overview/copyright/}
\item Credits and acknowledgements page of the Webonary dictionary. \url{https://www.webonary.org/vagla/overview/credits-acknowledgements/}
\item Glottolog reference for Crouch and Herbert 1981. \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/reference/id/126353}
\item Vagla language (Wikipedia): tones and phonology overview. \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vagla_language}
\item Omniglot page on the Vagla writing system. \url{https://www.omniglot.com/writing/vagla.htm}
\end{itemize}
No detailed official orthography document was found.
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item UNESCO language profile: reports GILLBT has worked on Vagla since 1962 and translated the Old and New Testaments (secondary source; verify). \url{https://ar.wal.unesco.org/index.php/en/countries/ghana/languages/vagla}
\item Omniglot sample of Vagla text from the Bible. \url{https://www.omniglot.com/babel/vagla.htm}
\end{itemize}
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
The Webonary dictionary is the main digital resource found. No audio was found.
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Vagla is not known to be taught in schools. The GILLBT dictionary and Bible translation provide a basis for orthography-based reading materials; details should be confirmed with GILLBT.
\end{document}
